{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Like sheep, they are set</b> — like: \"their mouth is set in the heavens.\" The meaning: they set themselves in their thought that they are like sheep." "<b>Death shall shepherd them</b> — for their end is slaughter." "<b>And the upright shall descend upon them</b> — this is after their death, and they are four elements that are not compounded: that the fire compounded in it returns to the fire, and the spirit to the spirit, and the waters to the waters, and the bones, which are of the nature of dust, to the dust." "<b>Meaning of \"for the morning\"</b> — corresponding to \"shall lodge.\" And the meaning: after midday they shall consume." "<b>And their rock</b> — like \"and their forms,\" and similar to it: \"their carved images\" [as if] כתבונתם. The meaning: that Sheol, which is below, where the body is — there the form will be consumed." "<b>And the meaning of \"from his dwelling\"</b> — from the dwelling that each one dwells in, from there will come to him the consumption. And R. Moses said: for if you omit the word \"those who rule\" and \"the upright,\" men will not be able to escape. And R. Jonah said: \"from his dwelling\" — the judgment of heaven upon each one."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {5 "The word מזבול ('his dwelling') appears in the verse; Ibn Ezra reads it as a noun meaning dwelling/place. The quoted interpretations from R. Moses and R. Jonah are rendered literally; their arguments remain compressed as in the original."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:24.570527425Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}